# interactor-tool-godot-cage-deformer

A Godot extension that deforms a mesh with a triangle cage using biharmonic coordinates.

## What it is for

It adds a mesh node that follows a coarse triangle cage, so moving the cage's vertices bends the detailed mesh inside it. The demo project lets the cage's vertices be dragged with handles in the editor.

## Build and run

    scons

This builds the extension into the demo project; open `demo/` in the Godot editor.

## Licence

MIT; see `LICENSE.md`. The biharmonic coordinates implementation is research code published with "Biharmonic Coordinates and their Derivatives for Triangular 3D Cages" by Jean-Marc Thiery, Elie Michel and Jiong Chen (SIGGRAPH 2024); its authors ask that any use acknowledge and cite that paper, as `LICENSE.biharmonic_3d` states. The demo's vertex-handle gizmo is by celyk.
